  "title": "How to keep babies and toddlers safe from RSV, Flu, and Winter Germs: Tips from a Pediatrician",
  "summary": "As the winter season approaches, cold weather drives people indoors where germs spread more easily, increasing the risk of viruses like RSV and the flu for young children. To keep your baby or toddler healthy, pediatricians recommend five key preventative strategies alongside knowing when to seek medical help: handwashing, sanitizing hotspots, boosting immunity with healthy foods, getting time outside, creating a protective plan",
